    "id": "pqueue-103570d4",
    "title": "Validate ESF entity schemas before every pqueue write",
    "description": "Compile QueueDefinition.entity_schema once per queue and validate typed item documents pre-commit on every write path. Previous attempt left blocking gaps: push and push_with_request_id paths in sqlite log, postgres log, objectlog, sqlite relational, postgres relational, and object-log composite/server paths can still build PushItems and commit without validate_entity; sqlite relational vectorized commit lifecycle_items can apply Push without schema validation. Fix those gaps. Rejection must happen before log append, object-log append, idempotency recording, SQL mutation, projection apply, or vectorized commit entry effects. In-scope files: pqueue-engine schema validation helpers, memory/sqlite/postgres/objectlog push/request-id implementations, sqlite/postgres relational push implementations, pqueue-server object_log_sqlite composite implementations, sqlite relational commit lifecycle path, conformance/backend tests. Out-of-scope: secondary index key replacement.",
    "acceptance": "cargo test -p pqueue schema_validation -- --nocapture passes; cargo test -p pqueue-conformance storage_conformance -- --nocapture passes; backend-specific tests prove invalid entity push and push_with_request_id reject before durable mutation/idempotency on memory, sqlite log, sqlite relational, objectlog, object_log_sqlite composite paths, and env-gated postgres paths where available; sqlite relational vectorized commit with invalid lifecycle_items rejects the entry without creating lifecycle items; rg -n 'build_push_items|record_push_idempotency|commit_command|append' crates/pqueue-sqlite/src crates/pqueue-postgres/src crates/pqueue-objectlog/src crates/pqueue-server/src/object_log_sqlite.rs shows validation immediately before push/request-id durable mutation sites.",
